  - frames are a `List Nat` whose order gives the parent and the ancestor;
  - `ExercisableAt` reads the stack only through its top;
  - WF3, I1–I3, NoDangling and NoOrphan read the stack only through membership.
- Concurrent state `SC`:
  - `Ctx` holds the stack, `Life` (live | done) and the parent of the initial frame;
  - `view s c` is c's stack followed by the other live frames;
  - `flat` lists all live frames;
  - `set` writes back the kernel fields;
  - `parC` and `ancestorC` follow `chain` over decreasing ids (Spec 1 §49, last paragraph).
- Re-indexed ops `opStepC`:
  - ops that do not read the ancestor relation go through `ViewStep`;
  - re-indexed C-structures for transfer, depend, store, enter and exit.
- Frame ops: `exitFrameC` is O7 plus reparenting; `spawnEff`/`SpawnPreBase`; `termEffC`/`TermPre`; `JoinStep` (waiting means no outcome).
